	// ValidatePipelineWithBody Validate a pipeline spec
	//
	// Validates a pipeline spec against one enabled project environment. This is the shared validation surface for frontend builder preflight and CLI server-target validation. Validation applies the canonical pipeline spec validator: syntax/schema decoding, required fields, supported step kinds, graph and binding consistency, source/sink/transform target shape, and mutually exclusive operation references. Server validation resolves logical data-source refs through the selected project environment and rejects sink replay policies unsupported by the resolved connector before checking org-scoped cached data-source schema metadata when the spec contains contracts or transforms that require schema context. It does not refresh schemas, call live connectors, run operations, or prove that referenced connector operations exist in the target environment. Failed validation results with a pipeline slug are stored as non-run diagnostic history for operator triage only when the caller is authorized to update pipeline history; the response body remains the source of truth for validation semantics. UI builder validation may still run earlier local checks for draft completeness and graph editing feedback; CLI --local validation uses the local validator without contacting this endpoint and therefore cannot check bindings or cached server-side schema metadata.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /organizations/{slug}/projects/{project_slug}/environments/{environment_slug}/pipeline-validation (the `ValidatePipeline` operationId).
